      "statusChangeID": "6a4d57c1ec0c188090921315",
      "statusChangeNewStatus": "closed",
      "value": "Thanks for your feedback. At this time, we are not planning to allow more than one active companion at a time per user. There are a few reasons for this:\n\n- Limiting to one companion per user allows us to increase the network update rate for companions compared to standard items, since it bounds the total amount of network traffic that can be generated by companions.\n\n- It also limits the worst case performance impact of companions, allowing us to do more complex things with them compared to standard items.\n\n- Having multiple companions per user would likely introduce an expectation for local avoidance so these companions don't move through each other, which would further increase the performance cost.\n\n- Limiting companions may improve social legibility and avoid clutter, since companions are intended as a small extension of the user and their avatar, and we're trying to avoid having large swarms of companions following behind everyone.\n\nWe appreciate this might be frustrating, but hopefully this gives some context about why the system is currently set up the way it is. Thanks again.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
